## Settings → Slideshow
settings-section-slideshow = Slideshow
settings-slideshow-interval = Time per image
settings-slideshow-interval-help = How long each image stays on screen. Animations play through once, up to a minute.
settings-slideshow-shuffle = Shuffle
settings-slideshow-shuffle-help = Show the images in a random order. Every image appears once before any comes back.
settings-slideshow-repeat = Loop
settings-slideshow-repeat-help = Start again after the last image instead of stopping.
settings-slideshow-include-subfolders = Include subfolders
settings-slideshow-include-subfolders-help = Show the images in subfolders of the folder as well.
settings-slideshow-transition = Transition
settings-slideshow-transition-help = How one image gives way to the next. Ken Burns slowly pans and zooms; it is off when reduced motion is on.
settings-slideshow-transition-none = None
settings-slideshow-transition-cross-fade = Cross-fade
settings-slideshow-transition-ken-burns = Ken Burns
settings-slideshow-caption = Caption
settings-slideshow-caption-help = Text shown in a corner of each image.
settings-slideshow-caption-off = None
settings-slideshow-caption-name = File name
settings-slideshow-caption-name-exif = File name, date, camera and exposure

## Multi-monitor: the slideshow on another display, the viewer on another display.
settings-slideshow-monitor = Display
settings-slideshow-monitor-help = Where a slideshow plays. Automatic picks a display other than the one with the main window, so the main window stays free; with one display, the slideshow fills the main window.
settings-slideshow-monitor-auto = Automatic
settings-monitor-not-connected = Not connected
palette-viewer-other-monitor = Show the viewer on another display
presenting-on = Presenting on { $display }
presenting-viewer-on = Viewer on { $display }
presenting-pause = Pause slideshow
presenting-resume = Resume slideshow
presenting-stop = Stop slideshow
presenting-close-viewer = Close the viewer on the other display
toast-no-other-display = There is no other display connected
toast-display-disconnected = The display { $display } was disconnected
slideshow-started-on = Slideshow started on { $display }
viewer-on-display = Showing the viewer on { $display }
viewer-on-display-closed = Closed the viewer on the other display
toast-display-moved = The display { $old } was disconnected; now presenting on { $display }
